# Walkthrough for the MVC demo (controller-based twin of the minimal-API demo).
# Runnable from Visual Studio 2022 or VS Code (REST Client extension).
#
# Start the app first:
#   ASPNETCORE_URLS=http://localhost:5199 dotnet run --project samples/PostQuantum.Identity.Mvc.Demo

@base = http://localhost:5199

### 1. Register — Argon2id-hashed password.
POST {{base}}/account/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "ada", "password": "Lovelace#1843" }

### 2. Login — ML-DSA-65–signed PQ-JWT.
# @name login
POST {{base}}/account/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "ada", "password": "Lovelace#1843" }

### 3. Protected controller endpoint.
GET {{base}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 4. Refresh — new token first, then the old jti is revoked.
# @name refresh
POST {{base}}/account/refresh
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 4a. Old token -> expect 401.
GET {{base}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 5. Logout with the new token.
POST {{base}}/account/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{refresh.response.body.$.token}}

### 5a. Token after logout -> expect 401.
GET {{base}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{refresh.response.body.$.token}}
